# Fuel economy: mpg

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:giggly, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
  ])
```

## About this notebook

ggplot2's reference page for [`mpg`](https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/mpg.html) has no
examples, so this notebook says only what the page describes and where Giggly stands.

`mpg` is a subset of the fuel economy data the US EPA publishes at fueleconomy.gov: 234 cars of
38 models, kept because each had a new release every year from 1999 to 2008, which stands in for
their popularity. Each row gives a car's manufacturer and model, its engine displacement in
litres, year of manufacture, number of cylinders, transmission, drive train (`f` front-wheel, `r`
rear-wheel, `4` four-wheel), city and highway miles per gallon, fuel type and class. Giggly has it
as `Giggly.Datasets.mpg/0`, which returns ggplot2's `mpg` as a keyword list of columns, a table
`Giggly.Plot.new/2` takes as it is.
